# =====================================================================
# Data — track curated model INPUTS, ignore large / regeneratable / legacy
# =====================================================================
# Tracked (NOT ignored): data/dna, data/current_rosters, data/external
#   — JSON/CSV inputs the Python engine actually consumes.
# Ignored below: regeneratable caches, runtime state, and legacy R data.
# Ignored below (2026-07-22): a handful of data/dna and data/current_rosters
#   files that ARE large AND fully, deterministically regeneratable by
#   scripts/roster_management/regenerate_dna_v_0_1_0.py (run that after a
#   fresh clone). Everything else in data/dna/current_rosters stays tracked
#   — either it's small, or it contains real hand-curated judgment (rookie
#   projections, coach maps, trench_tiers estimates) with no regeneration
#   script, or (trench_dna.json specifically) part of its content depends on
#   an unverified upstream chain — see regenerate_dna_v_0_1_0.py's docstring.
# NOTE: .gitignore does NOT support trailing/inline comments — every pattern
# must be alone on its line, or the comment becomes part of the pattern.

# Regenerate via scripts/roster_management/regenerate_dna_v_0_1_0.py
data/dna/qb_dna.json
data/dna/rb_dna.json
data/dna/wr_dna.json
data/dna/te_dna.json
data/dna/skill_dna.json
data/dna/coach_dna.json
data/current_rosters/*_traits_2026.json

# 295MB training-master CSV + pools (regenerated from nflverse pulls)
data/processed/
# sim-result parquet caches + per-week JSON (regenerated by sim runners)
data/interim/
# runtime bot state (bot_state.db) + live game CSV output
data/live/
data/cache/
# legacy R training splits (.rds) — superseded by joblib model artifacts
data/win_probability/
data/field_goal/
data/fourth_down/

# Model training caches (regenerated on next train run)
*_train_cache.parquet

# =====================================================================
# Legacy archive — keep CODE for reference, ignore superseded DATA/binaries
# =====================================================================
# legacy/ retains the old R/Python implementation as a readable reference
# archive (~6k lines of code). Its data + model binaries (2.35GB, incl. 9
# files over GitHub's 100MB hard limit) are superseded and regeneratable —
# excluded, same principle as the active data/processed/.
legacy/data/
legacy/models_archive/
legacy/**/*.npy
legacy/**/*.pt

Notebooks
R/logs

# R basics
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rapp.history
.Renviron


# renv
renv/
renv.lock.bak


# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# active project virtualenv (Python 3.12) — reproduce via requirements.txt
venv/
.venv/
# temporary fallback from the 3.8->3.12 upgrade; delete once 3.12 is trusted
venv_py38_old/
# Isolated venv for the cfbd package (2026-08-20) -- cfbd pins pydantic<2,
# which conflicts with the main venv's pydantic 2.x (FastAPI backend needs
# 2.x) if installed into the same environment. Keep it fully separate.
venv_cfbd/
.pytest_cache/


# Local secrets & runtime
.env
logs/
R/bots/.posted_keys.rds
# Live bot per-game runtime output (regenerated each run; keep only the README)
R/bots/live_csv/*.csv
R/bots/live_csv/*.log


# Data cache & artifacts
*.duckdb
*.sqlite


# OneDrive multi-machine sync-conflict duplicates — stale copies of real files
# (e.g. game_engine-Cams-Desktop.py). Never commit; delete from disk when found.
*-Cams-Desktop.*

# OS/editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.obsidian/
scratch/

# Local pre-change checkpoints (2026-09-06) -- large, machine-specific, not for git
data/_snapshots/

# Week-by-week roster trees for the season sim -- 18x32 files, always
# regeneratable via build_season_week_rosters_v_0_1_0.py
data/current_rosters/week_*/

# Live-blend sanity-check sheets -- regenerated every refresh_weekly_dna_v_0_1_0.py
# run (export_live_week_overrides_v_0_1_0.py), mirrors week_NN/{TEAM}.csv but
# pulled from current_rosters/*_traits_2026.json instead of the frozen baseline.
data/overrides/2026/week_*/*_live.csv

# DFS ownership archive -- ignore every raw DK standings CSV (a 150-max milly
# export is 40 MB / 240k rows of contest-entrant data, and re-downloadable),
# whatever it's named (<name>_<price>_<xmax>max.csv). Keep the manifests, the
# pre-lock salary snapshots, and the processed parquets -- those are the small,
# curated model inputs. See data/dfs_ownership/README.md.
data/dfs_ownership/**/*.csv
!data/dfs_ownership/**/salaries_prelock.csv

# Local dev-server logs (backend_dfs*.log, frontend_dfs*.log at repo root)
*.log

# pip install -e build metadata from pyproject.toml
*.egg-info/

# DFS optimizer run snapshots -- one 100-700 KB JSON per optimizer run, pure
# history. state.json (the current optimizer state) stays tracked.
data/optimizer/**/builds/

# Game Explorer workspace save slots -- rewritten on every UI save (3+ MB each),
# local working state only; nothing in history needs them.
data/workspace/
